This project has been created as part of the 42 curriculum by diogribe, nogioni-.

This project is inspired by the world-famous game Wolfenstein 3D, which is considered the first FPS ever created.
It allowed us to explore ray-casting.

Our goal was to create a dynamic view within a maze, where you need to find your way around.

Compile:
make
./cub3D "map file .cub"

Movement:
W and S to walk
A and D to strafe
left and right arrow to spin/look around

Resources and Tools:
[Raycasting Explained](https://lodev.org/cgtutor/raycasting.html)
[Minilibx Linux](https://github.com/42paris/minilibx-linux)
AI for general questions.